ne of them is always wrong: a chair has shifted, a light burns the wrong colour, a figure stands where nobody remembers one. The player carries no weapon, only a sonic ring that marks an anomaly. Firing it at the wrong thing carries sound through the floor and wakes the nearest Crawler, which then knows where the player is standing. Over 100 Crawlers inhabit these floors and no two of them share a rule, and room laws rewrite darkness, direction, distance, time and the mirrored views themselves. 100 named floors and 1,000 procedurally recombined rooms can be played alone or online with up to three other players.", "themes": [{"id": 19, "name": "Horror"}, {"id": 20, "name": "Thriller"}, {"id": 21, "name": "Survival"}, {"id": 43, "name": "Mystery"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/mirror-backrooms"}